---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
// Update this date whenever the terms change. It is shown on the page.
const UPDATED = 'October 11, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The rules for using Long Press: what the site is, what it is not, how you can quote it, and where disputes go. Last updated October 11, 2026."
>
  <div class="legal">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Terms</span>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        Reading Long Press is free. These are the few rules that come with it.
      </p>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="agreement">Using the site</h2>
      <p>
        By using longpress.news you agree to these terms and to the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the site. Long Press is published by Swami Guru under BuiltBySwami.
      </p>

      <h2 id="what-it-is">What Long Press is, and is not</h2>
      <p>
        Long Press publishes news, analysis and opinion about consumer technology. It is information, not professional advice. Fine Print explains rules and notices in plain language, and it is not legal advice. Buy, skip and wait verdicts in Known Issue are opinion, not financial advice. Prices, plans and availability change, so check the source before you spend money or act on a rule.
      </p>

      <h2 id="accuracy">Accuracy and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        The desk works to get facts right and fixes mistakes on the page. How corrections work, and how to report one, is on the <a href="/about#corrections-and-contact">About page</a> and in the <a href="/editorial-policy">Editorial Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="your-use">Using what Long Press publishes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You may read, share and link to any page.</li>
        <li>You may quote a short passage with credit to Long Press and a link to the page it came from.</li>
        <li>You may not republish full stories, cards or graphics, or present them as your own.</li>
        <li>You may not scrape the site at a rate that slows it down for others. The RSS feed is there for readers and feed apps.</li>
        <li>You may not suggest that Long Press endorses you, your product or your service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="ownership">Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The text, graphics, social cards, the Long Press name and its mark belong to Long Press and BuiltBySwami. Names of companies and products mentioned in stories belong to their owners and appear only to identify them.
      </p>

      <h2 id="links">Links and third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Long Press links to other sites, including the WhatsApp channel. It does not control them and is not responsible for what they publish or how they handle your data.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ads">Ads and sponsors</h2>
      <p>
        Ads are labeled "Advertisement". Paid content is labeled as paid. An ad or sponsor on the site is not an endorsement unless a page says so. More on this is in the <a href="/editorial-policy#money">Editorial Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="liability">No warranty and limit of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site and everything on it is provided as is, with no promise that it is complete, current or always available. To the extent the law allows, Long Press and its publisher are not liable for any loss that results from using the site or acting on what is published.
      </p>

      <h2 id="law">Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of India. Courts in Bengaluru have jurisdiction over any dispute.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        The date at the top changes whenever these terms do. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:builtbyswami@gmail.com">builtbyswami@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
